          <declname>original_size</declname>
          <defval>0</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Decode the original blob from a subset of shards.</para>
<para>Reconstruction succeeds as long as at least <computeroutput>data_shards</computeroutput> shards are available (i.e. up to <computeroutput>parity_shards</computeroutput> simultaneous failures are tolerated).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>blob_id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Identifier used for logging / error messages. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>shards</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Map of shard_index → <ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1storage_1_1_encoded_shard" kindref="compound">EncodedShard</ref> for every available (non-erased) shard. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>original_size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Expected original blob size in bytes. If zero, the value stored in the first available shard is used. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Reconstructed original data. </para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::runtime_error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if fewer than data_shards shards are present. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
