    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1storage_1_1_erasure_coding_backend" kindref="compound">ErasureCodingBackend</ref></para>
<para>Self-contained backend that encodes blobs into Reed-Solomon stripes and reconstructs them from any k-of-(k+m) available shards. Storage of the encoded shards is handled by the caller; this class provides only the encode/decode logic and an optional in-memory shard store for testing.</para>
<para>Thread-safety: all public methods are thread-safe.</para>
<para>Usage example (RS 10+4): <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">ErasureCodingConfig<sp/>cfg;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cfg.data_shards<sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/>10;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">cfg.parity_shards<sp/>=<sp/>4;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemisdb_1_1storage_1_1_erasure_coding_backend_1a1e434b6d63e7685ca87af9a26d12ef15" kindref="member">ErasureCodingBackend</ref><sp/>backend(cfg);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">backend.put(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;blob-123&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>data);<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>encode<sp/>+<sp/>store<sp/>internally</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>recovered<sp/>=<sp/>backend.get(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;blob-123&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>reconstruct<sp/>from<sp/>shards</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
